{"name":"Leap of Faith","hex":"#c4d3e3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"leap of faith","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of believing in something despite a lack of proof of its truth or existence, or the attempt of something without being sure of its possible outcome."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leap_of_faith"}],"entries":[{"title":"Leap of Faith (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Leap of Faith is a 1992 American comedy-drama film directed by Richard Pearce and starring Steve Martin, Debra Winger, Lolita Davidovich, Liam Neeson, and Lukas Haas. The film is about Jonas Nightengale, a Christian faith healer who uses his revival meetings to milk money out of the inhabitants of Rustwater, Kansas."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/98/Leap_of_faith_film.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leap_of_Faith_(film)","wikidata":"Q1196673"},{"title":"Leap of Faith (musical)","blocks":[{"text":"Leap of Faith is a stage musical based on the 1992 American movie of the same name, which starred Steve Martin. The music is by Alan Menken, with lyrics by Glenn Slater and a book by Janus Cercone and Warren Leight about a con man posing as a man of faith, who is redeemed by the love of a good woman."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/74/Leap_of_Faith_Broadway_Playbill_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leap_of_Faith_(musical)","wikidata":"Q6509938"},{"title":"Leap of faith","blocks":[{"text":"In philosophy, a leap of faith is the act of believing in or accepting something not on the basis of reason. The phrase is commonly associated with Danish philosopher Søren Kierkegaard."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leap_of_faith","wikidata":"Q3243516"},{"title":"Faith","blocks":[{"text":"In religion, faith is the \"belief in God or in the doctrines or teachings of religion\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Faith","wikidata":"Q5410500"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Kierkegaard_portrait.jpg/500px-Kierkegaard_portrait.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Kierkegaard_portrait.jpg/500px-Kierkegaard_portrait.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Kierkegaard at his desk","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKierkegaard_portrait.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/National_gallery_in_washington_d.c.%2C_mino_da_fiesole%2C_fede%2C_1475-1480.JPG/500px-National_gallery_in_washington_d.c.%2C_mino_da_fiesole%2C_fede%2C_1475-1480.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/National_gallery_in_washington_d.c.%2C_mino_da_fiesole%2C_fede%2C_1475-1480.JPG/500px-National_gallery_in_washington_d.c.%2C_mino_da_fiesole%2C_fede%2C_1475-1480.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Faith (Armani), by Mino da Fiesole ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANational_gallery_in_washington_d.c.%2C_mino_da_fiesole%2C_fede%2C_1475-1480.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Triumph_of_Faith_over_Idolatry_Theodon.jpg/500px-Triumph_of_Faith_over_Idolatry_Theodon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Triumph_of_Faith_over_Idolatry_Theodon.jpg/1280px-Triumph_of_Faith_over_Idolatry_Theodon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Triumph_of_Faith_over_Idolatry_Theodon.jpg/500px-Triumph_of_Fait